and  │\n│ • Autonomy Posture: `approval_mode: \"yolo\"` (autonomous)    │ • Autonomy Posture: `approval_mode: \"always_ask\"` (HITL)    │\n│ • Workspace Canvas: Live Edge Website Preview + MRR Radar   │ • Workspace Canvas: Domain-Specific Viewports (Redline/Grid)│\n│ • Telephony/Channels: Public inbound customer receptionist  │ • Telephony/Channels: Mobile Executive Chief of Staff       │\n│ • Sleep Lifecycle: Standing 24/7 loops \u0026 scheduled wakes    │ • Sleep Lifecycle: Finite task sleep (hibernates on 100%)   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\n## 2. Ingestion Layer: Cohere Parse 5 (`parse-v5.0`) at the Edge\n\nVertical Cowork spaces must process messy, multi-column enterprise scans, faxes, and complex tables without OCR hallucination.\n- Integrate Cohere Parse 5 (2.3B Vision-Language Model) directly into `workers/knowledge/src/parse5Ingestion.ts`.\n- Ingest raw document bytes from Cloudflare R2, call `https://api.cohere.com/v2/parse`, and stream clean Markdown directly into the project\u0027s SQLite virtual filesystem (`workspace_files`) and Cloudflare AI Search.\n- Use Parse 5 Markdown output as the authoritative source for downstream legal redlining, financial modeling, and clinical SOAP generation.\n\n## 3. Four Core Vertical Cowork Blueprints\n\nImplement the declarative definitions for four turnkey vertical spaces:\n\n1. \"Harvey for Law\" — Corporate M\u0026A \u0026 Litigation Studio (`tpl_lexpulse_legal_v1`):\n   - Target: Boutique law firms, General Counsels.\n   - Core Projects:\n     * `doc_studio` (Contract Redline Canvas with Delaware statutory linter).\n     * `knowledge_vault` (Litigation discovery transcripts indexed in Cloudflare AI Search).\n     * `regulatory_radar` (State/federal statutory updates via Kitesurf).\n   - Ingestion: Scanned 100-page commercial leases, historical deeds, and indemnification matrices.\n   - Pricing: $299 / month.\n\n2. \"Harvey for Finance\" — Private Equity \u0026 Deal Studio (`tpl_capforge_pe_v1`):\n   - Target: Investment bankers, PE associates, fractional CFOs.\n   - Core Projects:\n     * `finance_grid` (SpreadsheetFormulaGrid with interactive formula engine).\n     * `sec_rag` (SEC EDGAR 10-K/10-Q filing ingestion and EBITDA adjustment reconciler).\n     * `memos` (Automated investment memo compiler).\n   - Ingestion: Trailing 12-Month statements (T-12s), commercial rent rolls, pitch decks.\n   - Pricing: $299 / month.\n\n3. \"Harvey for Healthcare\" — Clinical Chart \u0026 EHR Desk (`tpl_clinica_ehr_v1`):\n   - Target: Medical practices, dental networks, physical therapy clinics.\n   - Core Projects:\n     * `clinical_soap` (ClinicalSoapEditor with HIPAA-compliant PII scrubber).\n     * `billing_codes` (ICD-10 and CPT code matching engine).\n     * `pre_auth` (Insurance prior-authorization appeal letter generator).\n   - Ingestion: Hospital fax transmissions, printed diagnostic lab panels.\n   - Pricing: $249 / month (Air-Gapped / Zero-Egress mode enabled).\n\n4. \"Harvey for Construction\" — Plan Spec \u0026 Permitting Studio (`tpl_acubuild_const_v1`):\n   - Target: General contractors, civil engineering firms, commercial builders.\n   - Core Projects:\n     * `plan_spec` (PlanSpecCanvas schematic inspection viewport).\n     * `code_compliance` (Municipal zoning code vector index).\n     * `bid_matrix` (Subcontractor RFP price normalizer).\n   - Ingestion: 300-page architectural specification manuals, municipal amendments.\n   - Pricing: $249 / month.\n\n## 4. Multi-Player Document Collaboration (OCC + Cloudflare Artifacts)\n\nDo not use uncoordinated CRDT libraries. Enforce document collaboration using the platform\u0027s native storage hierarchy:\n- Primary State: Authoritative SQLite virtual filesystem inside `SpaceDO` (`workspace_files`).\n- In-Memory Consistency: Single-threaded Durable Object execution loop enforces Optimistic Concurrency Control (OCC) using SHA-256 hash checks (`WHERE path \u003d ? AND hash \u003d base_hash`).\n- Versioning \u0026 History: Every save turn or milestone triggers a commit to Cloudflare Artifacts (Git for Agents via Zig-WASM in DO).\n- Teammate Awareness: Broadcast file mutations and presence cursors over `WsHubDO` WebSockets.\n\n## 5. Declarative Blueprint Schema (`packages/types/src/blueprint.ts`)\n\nExport the unified TypeScript interface defining blueprints:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface BusinessBlueprint {\n  id: string; // e.g. \"tpl_lexpulse_legal_v1\"\n  title: string;\n  category: \"LEGAL\" | \"FINANCE\" | \"HEALTHCARE\" | \"CONSTRUCTION\" | \"AGENCY\" | \"MICRO_SAAS\";\n  template_mode: \"autonomous_venture\" | \"vertical_cowork\";\n  description: string;\n  version: string;\n  author: {\n    userId: string;\n    name: string;\n    royaltyRate: number; // 0.40 for referral, 0.20 for organic\n  };\n  \n  // Specific configurations for Vertical Cowork mode\n  cowork_config?: {\n    defaultViewport: \"DocumentRedlineCanvas\" | \"SpreadsheetFormulaGrid\" | \"ClinicalSoapEditor\" | \"PlanSpecCanvas\";\n    enforceCitationFootnotes: boolean;\n    auditLogRetentionDays: number; // 365 for HIPAA/SOC2 compliance\n    airGappedModeAvailable: boolean;\n  };\n\n  // Pre-configured projects in this space\n  projects: Array\u003c{\n    name: string;\n    slug: string;\n    kind: \"product_dev\" | \"doc_studio\" | \"voice_agent\" | \"customer_bot\" | \"model_studio\" | \"growth_engine\" | \"app_studio\";\n    viewportComponent: string;\n    allowedLadderTiers: Array\u003c1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 5 | 6\u003e;\n    defaultContainer?: string;\n    plugins: string[];\n    linterRules: string[];\n    initialJournalGoals: Array\u003c{ id: string; title: string; dependencies?: string[] }\u003e;\n  }\u003e;\n\n  // Domain Knowledge Seeds (Pre-indexed into Cloudflare AI Search)\n  knowledge_seeds: Array\u003c{\n    title: string;\n    content: string;\n    category: string;\n    sourceDocumentUrl?: string;\n  }\u003e;\n}\n```\n\nImplement the schema, the Parse 5 edge worker ingestion pipeline, and ensure the UI dynamically switches between Venture Mode (Live Preview + Revenue) and Cowork Mode (Domain Canvas + Citations) without backend fragmentation.\n```\n\n---\n\n# PROMPT 2: The 1-Click Blueprint Exporter, Marketplace \u0026 Settlement Rails\n*(Derived from `184 - 186 And.txt`, reconciled against the full platform architecture)*\n\n```markdown\n# SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE PROMPT: 1-CLICK BLUEPRINT EXPORTER \u0026 DEVELOPER MARKETPLACE\n\nYou are architecting the template export pipeline, developer distribution engine, and multi-party settlement rails for AVOS.\n\nTransform the platform into a self-scaling developer ecosystem where local programmers and domain experts package, publish, and monetize business blueprints and vertical cowork templates.\n\n## 1. The 1-Click \"Venture Exporter\" Pipeline\n\nDevelopers build and test their business or cowork spaces live inside the UI, then export them in one click. Implement `POST /spaces/:spaceId/export-template` in `workers/spaces/src/business-routes.ts`:\n\n1. Space Introspection:\n   - Call `SpaceDO` to export projects, installed plugins, Task DAGs, system directives (`SOUL.md`), domain linters, and SQLite starter files.\n\n2. PII \u0026 Vault Secret Sanitization:\n   - Physically strip all decrypted keys from `space_credentials`. Replace with declarative requirement placeholders: `{ \"requires_credential\": \"STRIPE_SECRET_KEY\", \"service\": \"stripe\" }`.\n   - Sanitize customer transaction logs, member email lists, phone numbers, and private chat histories.\n\n3. Deterministic Security \u0026 Stability Gate:\n   - Capability Validation: Verify that templates declaring `CUSTOMER_SUPPORT` roles do not contain hidden bindings to Container Tier 6 or filesystem modification tools.\n   - Injection Linter: Scan all prompt templates, `SOUL.md` files, and seed data for credential exfiltration tags or un-escaped script injection keywords.\n   - Isolated Sandbox Test: A Cloudflare Workflow boots the compiled blueprint in an ephemeral test DO, executes build/test checks, and issues an automated Safety Rating (0–100).\n\n4. Storage \u0026 Registration:\n   - Store the sanitized manifest at `blueprints/${blueprintId}.json` in Cloudflare R2 (`SCRIPTS_R2`).\n   - Insert listing record into `PLATFORM_DB` (Cloudflare D1) under `marketplace_listings`.\n\n## 2. Reconciled Monetization \u0026 Commission Rules\n\nDo not use flat 80/20 splits. Implement the exact reconciled marketplace economics:\n\n### A. The Three Distribution Channels\n1. Developer Direct Referral (Link/QR):\n   - Attribution: Client onboards via `app.platform.com/join?template\u003dtpl_102\u0026dev\u003dpartnerId`.\n   - Revenue Split: **40% Recurring to Developer / 60% to Platform**.\n2. Organic Marketplace Discovery:\n   - Attribution: Client discovers template in the platform directory.\n   - Revenue Split: **20% Recurring to Developer / 80% to Platform**.\n3. Fixed-Price One-Off License (Buy-Out):\n   - Pricing: Developer sets a one-time fee ($49 to $499).\n   - Revenue Split: **100% of upfront purchase to Developer / 0% on recurring monthly platform compute**.\n   - Platform keeps 100% of the ongoing base subscription ($29/mo) to cover edge infrastructure.\n\n### B. The Mutual Exclusivity Rule (Binary Marketplace Model)\n- Model 1: Freemium Tiered SaaS Template\n  * Upfront Install Price: **$0.00 (Free to install)**.\n  * Feature Gating: Developer gates features across $20, $50, and $150 plan tiers.\n  * Developer earns recurring monthly commissions as clients upgrade.\n- Model 2: Fixed One-Off License\n  * Upfront Install Price: **Fixed fee ($49 – $499)**.\n  * Feature Gating: **Prohibited**. All template features must be 100% unlocked forever.\n\n### C. Cumulative Per-Tier Cycle Quotas (Anti-Plan-Hopping)\nTo protect platform unit economics on low-priced plans while rewarding high-ticket retainers:\n- Entry Tier ($20/mo): Developer receives commission for **maximum 6 paid cycles ($48 total bounty)**. Drops to 0% thereafter (Platform captures 100%).\n- Growth Tier ($50/mo): Developer receives commission for **maximum 12 paid cycles ($240 total bounty)**. Drops to 0% thereafter.\n- Pro Tier ($150+/mo): **Lifetime recurring commission** for the duration of the client.\n- Cumulative Quota Tracking: Store separate cycle counters in D1 (`cycles_paid_entry_tier`, `cycles_paid_growth_tier`, `cycles_paid_pro_tier`). Switching back and forth between plans tracks cumulative cycles so developers cannot game the system.\n\n### D. Dynamic First-Month Price Floor\nEnforce that no template can be sold below cost:\n$$\\text{Minimum Month 1 Price} \u003d \\text{Platform Base Plan} + \\sum \\text{Plugin One-Time Wholesale Fees}$$\n\n## 3. Database Schema in Cloudflare D1 (`PLATFORM_DB`)\n\n```sql\n-- Developer Partner Accounts\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS partner_accounts (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                       -- e.g. \"dev_john_102\"\n  user_id TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  display_name TEXT NOT NULL,\n  payout_email TEXT NOT NULL,\n  payout_destination_json TEXT,              -- Stripe Connect / ACH details\n  total_earned_cents INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  balance_cents INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027))\n);\n\n-- Attributed Client Subscriptions with Cumulative Tier Quotas\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS template_subscriptions (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  space_id TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,\n  template_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  developer_user_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES partner_accounts(user_id),\n  attribution_channel TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (attribution_channel IN (\u0027DEVELOPER_REFERRAL\u0027, \u0027MARKETPLACE_ORGANIC\u0027, \u0027FIXED_ONE_OFF\u0027)),\n  \n  -- Cumulative Paid Cycles\n  cycles_paid_entry_tier INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,  -- Cap: 6 max\n  cycles_paid_growth_tier INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, -- Cap: 12 max\n  cycles_paid_pro_tier INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,    -- Unlimited\n\n  last_billed_plan_price_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT \u0027active\u0027 CHECK (status IN (\u0027active\u0027, \u0027paused\u0027, \u0027cancelled\u0027)),\n  updated_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027)),\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027))\n);\n\n-- Immutable Payout \u0026 Settlement Ledger\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS developer_earnings_ledger (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n  developer_user_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  space_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  event_type TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (event_type IN (\u0027subscription_cut\u0027, \u0027one_off_license_sale\u0027, \u0027plugin_sale\u0027)),\n  gross_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  developer_cut_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  platform_cut_cents INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  period TEXT NOT NULL,                              -- e.g. \"2026-08\"\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027))\n);\n```\n\n## 4. Automated Multi-Party Settlement Engine\n\nImplement `settleTemplateSubscriptionPayment()` in `workers/billing/src/settlement.ts`:\n- On every successful Stripe/Lemon Squeezy invoice webhook:\n  1. Fetch `template_subscriptions` for the paying `space_id`.\n  2. Increment the corresponding tier cycle counter based on `gross_cents`.\n  3. Evaluate commission eligibility:\n     * If `\u003c\u003d $25`: eligible only if `cycles_paid_entry_tier \u003c\u003d 6`.\n     * If `\u003c $150`: eligible only if `cycles_paid_growth_tier \u003c\u003d 12`.\n     * If `\u003e\u003d $150`: always eligible (Lifetime).\n  4. Compute split: 40% if `DEVELOPER_REFERRAL`, 20% if `MARKETPLACE_ORGANIC`, 0% if `FIXED_ONE_OFF` or quota exceeded.\n  5. Atomically record cuts in `developer_earnings_ledger` and update `balance_cents` in `partner_accounts`.\n\nEnsure the Partner Studio inside `apps/shell` renders live client rosters, remaining cycle counts, upgrade proposal triggers, and automated payout withdrawals.\n```",
