──────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3. Implementation on Cloudflare (`workers/agents/src/workspace.ts`)\n\n```typescript\nimport { Workspace } from \"@cloudflare/computer\";\nimport { Bash } from \"just-bash\";\n\nexport class AgentWorkspace {\n  private workspace: Workspace;\n  private virtualBash: Bash;\n\n  constructor(private doStorage: DurableObjectStorage) {\n    // 1. Authoritative SQLite Virtual Filesystem\n    this.workspace \u003d new Workspace({ storage: this.doStorage });\n\n    // 2. In-Memory Virtual Shell with Wasm Plugins\n    this.virtualBash \u003d new Bash({\n      fs: this.workspace.fs,\n      python: true,  // Embedded Pyodide CPython Wasm\n      sqlite: true,  // Embedded Wasm SQLite\n      network: { enabled: true, allowList: [\"api.stripe.com\", \"api.github.com\"] }\n    });\n  }\n\n  async exec(command: string, envVars: Record\u003cstring, string\u003e \u003d {}) {\n    const trimmed \u003d command.trim();\n\n    // 90%+ of commands run in V8 Isolate in sub-5ms ($0.00 compute cost)\n    if (this.isVirtualizable(trimmed)) {\n      const res \u003d await this.virtualBash.exec(trimmed, { env: envVars, cwd: \"/workspace\" });\n      return { stdout: res.stdout, stderr: res.stderr, exitCode: res.exitCode, backend: \"v8_isolate\" };\n    }\n\n    // Heavy native compilers (cargo, gcc, npm run build) escalate to Tier 6 Container over FUSE\n    return await this.workspace.runtime.exec(command, { backend: \"container\", cwd: \"/workspace\" });\n  }\n\n  private isVirtualizable(cmd: string): boolean {\n    const heavy \u003d [\"cargo\", \"gcc\", \"g++\", \"make\", \"docker\", \"rustc\", \"npm install\", \"npm run build\"];\n    return !heavy.includes(cmd.split(/\\s+/)[0]);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n--- END OF FILE 321 - 323 Virtual CLI \u0026 Container Command Virtualization.md ---\n```\n\n---\n\n### File 2: `324 - 326 Minimalist Action Space \u0026 Invisible Runtime Hypervisor.md`\n\n```markdown\n--- START OF FILE 324 - 326 Minimalist Action Space \u0026 Invisible Runtime Hypervisor.md ---\n\n324 - 326\nI did get so what happens to 6 tiers of execution ladder and shouldn\u0027t there be a more minimalistic way looking at the execution ladder plus the virtuals it feel more of too much let\u0027s try making so that the ai doesn\u0027t need too much instructions ie for cli commands the ais was already trained on most cli commands etc all we do is give it skills for some things like ctx.... And so on . Even we talked about tier 2 codemode it can also write its own cmds and even just scripts and tier 3 dynamic workflows it should know that it has access to itband can use it and also tier 4 and 5 and 6 and virtual cli . I don\u0027t know where an getting at here but basically I want to not confuse the ai but at the same time for it to have a full 6tier plus virtual cli power that it can almost do anything \n\n### 1. The Core Realization: \"Prompt Paralysis\"\n\nExposing 6 different tier tools (`exec_sqlite_fs`, `exec_isolate_codemode`, `exec_workflow`, `exec_kitesurf`, `exec_browser`, `exec_container_bash`) burns reasoning tokens and causes instruction drift. \n\nFoundation models were pre-trained on millions of standard terminal sessions. They already know how to write `grep`, `git`, `python`, `curl`, and `npm`.\n\n**The Solution: The Unified Terminal Façade (Single-Shell Illusion)**\n* **What the AI sees:** A minimalist 3-tool developer surface (`Bash`, `Read`, `Edit`) + 2 senses (`Browser`, `Delegate`).\n* **What Cloudflare runs:** An **invisible runtime hypervisor** underneath `Bash` that dynamically routes commands to the optimal compute tier.\n\n---\n\n### 2. The Minimalist Tool Surface\n\n```typescript\nexport interface MinimalistAgentTools {\n  // ── HANDS (Execution) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  Bash: {\n    description: \"Execute terminal commands, Virtual CLIs, scripts, and build tools.\";\n    paramet