      "text": "To transform your platform from a standard LLM coding wrapper into an engine that **genuinely rivals tools like Cursor, Windsurf, Augment, or Devin**, you need to solve two fundamental challenges:\n\n1. **How any custom workflow (like the two-pass Repomix chunking method) becomes a pluggable, reusable Agent Strategy.**\n2. **How to give coding plugins deep, vertical code intelligence (AST parsing, file dependency graphs, symbol tables, and incremental Merkle indexing) natively at Cloudflare\u0027s edge.**\n\nHere is the architectural blueprint to make coding plugins modular, deeply intelligent, and capable of competing with dedicated vertical AI coding systems.\n\n---\n\n# PART 1: The Pluggable Cognitive Strategy Engine\n\nIn top vertical systems, an \"agent\" is not just a system prompt with a while-loop. It is a **Cognitive Strategy Pipeline**. \n\nBy decoupling the **Universal Agent Kernel (`NaelaoAgentDO`)** from the **Execution Strategy**, any user or plugin developer can package a custom methodology—whether it’s your two-pass Repomix chunker, Test-Driven Development (TDD), or a hierarchical sub-tree refactor—into a **`CodingStrategy` module**.\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                    UNIVERSAL AGENT KERNEL (NaelaoAgentDO)                   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│                          PLUGGABLE STRATEGY RUNNER                          │\n│                                                                             │\n│  [ Strategy A: Repomix Chunked ]    [ Strategy B: Cursor Fast-LSP ]         │\n│  • Pass 1: Tree-sitter map          • Real-time AST symbol graph            │\n│  • Pass 2: Targeted file pack       • Direct surgical AST patch             │\n│  • Pass 3: Chunk-by-chunk commit    • In-memory compiler typecheck          │\n│                                                                             │\n│  [ Strategy C: Test-Driven TDD ]    [ Strategy D: Spec-to-DAG Compiler ]    │\n│  • Generates vitest suite first     • Dual-tier Frontier Planner +          │\n│  • Red -\u003e Green AST patching loop   • Anonymous Edge Workers                │\n└─────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                      │\n                                      ▼\n                        [ 6-Tier Execution Ladder ]\n```\n\n### The Strategy Interface (`packages/types/src/coding-strategy.ts`)\n\nA developer authors a coding strategy by implementing this standard contract:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface CodingAgentStrategy {\n  id: string; // e.g., \"strat_repomix_two_pass_v1\"\n  name: string;\n  description: string;\n\n  // 1. Context Selection Pipeline\n  // How this strategy prepares code for the LLM context window\n  selectContext: (params: {\n    userGoal: string;\n    workspace: WorkspaceContext;\n    ctx: AvosRuntimeContext;\n  }) \u003d\u003e Promise\u003c{\n    packedContext: string;\n    tokenCountEstimate: number;\n    targetedFiles: string[];\n  }\u003e;\n\n  // 2. Task Decomposition / Chunking\n  // Splits a massive goal into token-safe execution steps\n  planExecution: (params: {\n    goal: string;\n    context: string;\n    ctx: AvosRuntimeContext;\n  }) \u003d\u003e Promise\u003cArray\u003c{ id: string; title: string; spec: string }\u003e\u003e;\n\n  // 3. Execution Turn Loop\n  // How changes are executed, verified, and committed\n  executeStep: (params: {\n    step: { id: string; title: string; spec: string };\n    ctx: AvosRuntimeContext;\n  }) \u003d\u003e Promise\u003c{\n    success: boolean;\n    modifiedFiles: string[];\n    commitMessage: string;\n  }\u003e;\n\n  // 4. Verification Gate\n  // How the strategy proves the code is correct before advancing\n  verifyStep: (params: {\n    modifiedFiles: string[];\n    ctx: AvosRuntimeContext;\n  }) \u003d\u003e Promise\u003c{ passed: boolean; errorFeedback?: string }\u003e;\n}\n```\n\nWhen a user selects or installs a coding plugin (e.g., `\"plugin_repomix_flash_builder\"`), the project agent simply swaps its active strategy:\n```typescript\nawait ctx.project.setAgentStrategy(\"strat_repomix_two_pass_v1\");\n```\n\n---\n\n# PART 2: The Edge Code Intelligence Subsystem (Rivaling Cursor \u0026 Windsurf)\n\nWhy do Cursor and Windsurf feel so much smarter than generic LLMs? \n**They do not feed raw files blindly to an LLM.** They maintain a real-time **Code Knowledge Graph**:\n1. When you edit `interface User`, they know every file that imports `User`.\n2. They know the call hierarchy: `Function A -\u003e calls Function B -\u003e calls Function C`.\n3. They track file dependencies via language abstract syntax trees (ASTs).\n\nTo let developers build plugins that challenge these platforms, your base platform must provide an **Edge Code Intelligence Engine** built into the project\u0027s Durable Object.\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                 EDGE CODE INTELLIGENCE ENGINE (In SpaceDO)                   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. WebAssembly Tree-sitter (`web-tree-sitter`)                              │\n│    Runs inside the V8 Isolate. Parses TS, Python, Rust, Go, and HTML into    │\n│    AST syntax trees in \u003c3 milliseconds.                                     │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. Incremental Merkle Hash Graph                                            │\n│    Only re-indexes files whose SHA-256 hash changed. Zero full-repo scans.   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. DO SQLite Relational Symbol Graph (`code_graph.sqlite`)                  │\n│    Stores symbols, definitions, exports, and imports as queryable SQL tables│\n│    living directly in the Durable Object.                                   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4. Semantic Code Vector Index (Cloudflare Vectorize)                        │\n│    Embeds docstrings and function summaries for conceptual discovery.       │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### The Relational Code Graph Schema (`SpaceDO.ts` SQLite)\n\nInside `/.avos/indexes/code_graph.sqlite`, the platform maintains the dependency graph of the codebase:\n\n```sql\n-- Track all declared classes, functions, interfaces, and types\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS code_symbols (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                       -- e.g. \"sym_src_auth_ts_verifyToken\"\n  file_path TEXT NOT NULL,                   -- \"src/auth.ts\"\n  symbol_name TEXT NOT NULL,                 -- \"verifyToken\"\n  symbol_kind TEXT NOT NULL,                 -- \"function\" | \"interface\" | \"class\" | \"type\"\n  start_line INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  end_line INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  signature_text TEXT NOT NULL,              -- \"export function verifyToken(token: string): Promise\u003cUser\u003e\"\n  docstring TEXT,\n  file_hash TEXT NOT NULL,\n  updated_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027))\n);\n\n-- Track import/export dependencies between files\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS code_dependencies (\n  source_file TEXT NOT NULL,                 -- \"src/api/checkout.ts\"\n  target_file TEXT NOT NULL,                 -- \"src/auth.ts\"\n  imported_symbols_json TEXT NOT NULL,       -- [\"verifyToken\", \"User\"]\n  PRIMARY KEY (source_file, target_file)\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n# PART 3: The Unified `ctx.code` SDK Exposed to Plugins\n\nPlugin authors don’t need to write complex AST parsers from scratch. The platform exposes a high-level **Code Intelligence SDK** on the `ctx` object (`AVOS_SDK.d.ts`):\n\n```typescript\ndeclare namespace ctx.code {\n  /**\n   * Find where a symbol is defined across the entire codebase.\n   */\n  function findDefinition(symbolName: string): Promise\u003cArray\u003c{\n    filePath: string;\n    line: number;\n    signature: string;\n  }\u003e\u003e;\n\n  /**\n   * Find all files and lines that import or call this symbol (Impact Analysis).\n   */\n  function findReferences(symbolName: string): Promise\u003cArray\u003c{\n    filePath: string;\n    line: number;\n    snippet: string;\n  }\u003e\u003e;\n\n  /**\n   * Get the direct dependency graph of a file (Upstream imports \u0026 Downstream callers).\n   */\n  function getFileDependencies(filePath: string): Promise\u003c{\n    imports: string[];\n    importedBy: string[];\n  }\u003e;\n\n  /**\n   * Native Context Packing Primitives (Available to any strategy)\n   */\n  namespace pack {\n    // Generates a Repomix-style compressed Tree-sitter outline of the repo\n    function compressedOutline(options?: { excludeGlobs?: string[] }): Promise\u003cstring\u003e;\n\n    // Packs a targeted slice: target file + the full signatures of its imports\n    function focusedSlice(targetFilePath: string): Promise\u003cstring\u003e;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Run in-memory TypeScript typecheck without starting a Docker container\n   */\n  function typecheck(): Promise\u003c{ passed: boolean; errors: Array\u003c{ file: string; line: number; message: string }\u003e }\u003e;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n# PART 4: How a Plugin Uses This to Build a \"Cursor Killer\"\n\nLook at how simple it becomes for a third-party developer to package an AI coding tool into a **Plugin Bundle** (`plugins/deep-coder/`):\n\n### 1. The Strategy Implementation (`plugins/deep-coder/strategy.ts`)\nWhen the user asks: *\"Refactor our billing database schema\"*, the plugin’s strategy doesn\u0027t dump the whole repo into Claude or Gemini:\n\n```typescript\nexport const DeepCoderStrategy: CodingAgentStrategy \u003d {\n  id: \"deep_coder_v1\",\n  name: \"DeepCoder Impact-Aware Refactorer\",\n  description: \"Refactors code by computing symbol dependency graphs before editing.\",\n\n  async selectContext({ userGoal, ctx }) {\n    // Step 1: Use Vectorize to find the core file related to the goal\n    const matches \u003d await ctx.code.findSymbols(\"BillingSchema\");\n    const coreFile \u003d matches[0]?.filePath || \"src/db/billing.ts\";\n\n    // Step 2: Query the Code Graph for all downstream callers!\n    const dependencies \u003d await ctx.code.getFileDependencies(coreFile);\n    \n    // Step 3: Automatically pack ONLY the core file + the signatures of its callers\n    const focusedContext \u003d await ctx.code.pack.focusedSlice(coreFile);\n\n    return {\n      packedContext: focusedContext,\n      targetedFiles: [coreFile, ...dependencies.importedBy],\n      tokenCountEstimate: 3500 // Super clean context window!\n    };\n  },\n\n  async executeStep({ step, ctx }) {\n    // Runs the surgical AST edit\n    await ctx.fs.edit(step.targetFile, step.oldStr, step.newStr);\n    \n    // Validates type safety in-memory\n    const check \u003d await ctx.code.typecheck();\n    if (!check.passed) {\n      throw new Error(`Typecheck failed: ${JSON.stringify(check.errors)}`);\n    }\n\n    return { success: true, modifiedFiles: [step.targetFile], commitMessage: step.title };\n  },\n\n  async verifyStep({ ctx }) {\n    // Runs local build verification in Tier 1/2 V8 or Tier 6 container\n    const testResult \u003d await ctx.cli.exec(\"npm test\");\n    return { passed: testResult.exitCode \u003d\u003d\u003d 0, errorFeedback: testResult.stderr };\n  }\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n# PART 5: What This Achieves for Your Marketplace\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Dimension                            │ Proprietary Tools (Cursor / Devin)   │ AVOS Coding Plugins                  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Architecture**                     │ Closed, rigid black-box pipeline     │ **Pluggable \u0026 Composable**           │\n│                                      │                                      │ (Swap strategies per project)        │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Code Intelligence**                │ Proprietary server daemons           │ **Edge-Native Code Graph**           │\n│                                      │ (Costly remote VM indexing)          │ (Tree-sitter Wasm + DO SQLite)       │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Context Efficiency**               │ Fixed heuristic chunking             │ **Developer Choice**                 │\n│                                      │                                      │ (Repomix map, symbol slice, call DAG)│\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Cost \u0026 Economics**                 │ $20 – $500 / seat / month            │ **$0 – $29 / month + BYOK**          │\n│                                      │                                      │ (Runs serverlessly on edge V8)       │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Monetization for Creators**        │ Zero (Platform keeps 100%)           │ **Creators sell custom strategies**  │\n│                                      │                                      │ ($10–$30 plugins or $150/mo spaces)  │\n└──────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Summary of What to Add to the Master Plan:\n1. **`CodingAgentStrategy` Contract:** Allows custom agent workflows (two-pass Repomix, TDD, symbol-slice) to be packaged as interchangeable strategies.\n2. **`code_graph.sqlite` in DO Memory:** Maintains real-time symbol definitions, imports, exports, and call hierarchies using `web-tree-sitter` in WebAssembly.\n3. **`ctx.code` SDK:** Empowers third-party plugin authors to build features like \"Find References\", \"Focused Slices\", and \"Impact Analysis\" with one line of code.\n4. **Instant Parity with Dedicated AI IDEs:** Anyone installing a coding plugin on your platform gets the deep static analysis of Cursor, the modularity of VS Code, and the execution speed of Cloudflare\u0027s serverless edge.",
