      "text": "This simplifies the entire architecture and eliminates a major trap. \n\nForcing developers to write bespoke TypeScript AST compilers, language servers, and custom execution loops creates **framework bloat, maintenance friction, and dangerous security vulnerabilities**. \n\nYour intuition to **turn indexers, dependency graphers, financial reconcilers, and legal cross-referencers into Sandboxed Background Gadgets (Micro-Apps)** makes the platform unified and secure.\n\nHere is how this works across **Code, Finance, and Legal**, and how users can customize the agent\u0027s execution steps with zero security risks.\n\n---\n\n# 1. The Core Architecture: Indexers \u0026 Graphers as \"Autonomous Gadgets\"\n\nIn AVOS, an indexer is **not** a complex plugin with low-level kernel hooks. \n\n**An indexer is simply a Stateful Gadget (Micro-App) running silently in the background:**\n* **Sandbox:** Runs inside an isolated **Dynamic Worker V8 Isolate** with its own **DO Facet SQLite database**.\n* **Security:** Bound by a **Gatekeeper Capability Grant** (it has read-only access to `/workspace` files and can only write to its own private SQLite database).\n* **Communication:** Automatically exposes an **MCP v2 (`/mcp`) endpoint**. The agent communicates with it using standard tool calls!\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                              THE BACKGROUND GADGET INDEXER MESH                                        │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ [ File Edited in Workspace (e.g. `src/auth.ts` or `invoices/Q3.csv`) ]                                 │\n│                                           │                                                            │\n│                                           ▼ (Event broadcast via WsHubDO)                              │\n│ ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│ │ 📱 BACKGROUND STATEFUL GADGET (Isolated Dynamic Worker + Private DO Facet SQLite)                  │ │\n│ │ • Parses the file diff silently in the background (sub-5ms).                                       │ │\n│ │ • Updates its private internal graph in DO Facet SQLite (`graph.sqlite`).                          │ │\n│ │ • Zero CPU or token overhead on the human\u0027s active chat!                                           │ │\n│ └─────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n│                                           │                                                            │\n│                                           ▼ (Auto-Exposes Stateless MCP v2 Endpoint)                   │\n│ ┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐ │\n│ │ ⚡ UNIVERSAL AGENT (NaelaoAgentDO)                                                                 │ │\n│ │ Calls the gadget natively via standard MCP: `mcp.call(\"code_graph\", \"find_impact\", { file })`      │ │\n│ └────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘ │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 2. This Works for ALL Verticals (Not Just Code)\n\nBecause an indexer is just a sandboxed Gadget that builds a private relational graph in SQLite, developers can package background intelligence for **any industry**:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                               VERTICAL GADGET INDEXERS (All Built the Same Way)                         │\n├───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Domain / Vertical             │ Background Gadget Name