ent doesn\u0027t need special hardcoded logic. \n\nThe agent sees the Gadget as an ordinary, high-IQ helper tool:\n\n### Example: The Agent Solving a Complex Coding Task\n1. User: *\"Refactor the User authentication schema.\"*\n2. Agent calls:\n   ```typescript\n   await ctx.mcp.call(\"code_graph\", \"get_file_impact\", { file: \"src/auth.ts\" });\n   ```\n3. The Background Gadget checks its private SQLite database and instantly replies in 2ms:\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"affectedFiles\": [\"src/api/login.ts\", \"src/api/checkout.ts\"],\n     \"exportedSymbols\": [\"verifyToken\", \"UserSession\"]\n   }\n   ```\n4. The agent now knows **exactly which 2 files to edit**, without searching or reading the entire repository!\n\n---\n\n# 4. Custom Harnesses: Safe Declarative Step Pipelines (No Dangerous Scripts)\n\nYou asked: *\"for custom harnesses user can sort of add steps or something without security issues?\"*\n\n**Yes.** To eliminate security risks, **never let users write raw execution loops or orchestrators**. \n\nInstead, allow users/templates to define **Declarative Step Pipelines (Hooks)** in `PROJECT.md` or the Project Template:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                 SAFE DECLARATIVE STEP PIPELINE (No Code Needed)             │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1. PRE-TURN HOOK (Context Enrichment):                                      │\n│    • Query specified Gadget via MCP before touching any files.              │\n│    • e.g. Call `code_graph` or `ledger_reconciler` to get relevant context. │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2. ACTION STEP (Universal Execution):                                       │\n│    • Agent applies standard `Edit` patch or writes solution.                │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3. POST-TURN HOOK (Verification Gate):                                      │\n│    • Run a declarative validation check before marking the task done:       │\n│      - Coding: `npm test` or typecheck                                      │\n│      - Finance: `reconcile_check --tolerance 0.01`                          │\n│      - Legal: `delaware_statute_check --strict`                             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### The Declarative Configuration in `blueprint.json`\n\nA developer building a \"Top AI Coding Studio\" or a \"Forensic Accounting Desk\" configures the pipeline with simple JSON:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"project_kind\": \"product_dev\",\n  \"installed_gadgets\": [\n    \"gadget_code_graph_v1\"\n  ],\n  \"agent_execution_pipeline\": {\n    \"pre_flight_mcp\": [\n      {\n        \"server\": \"gadget_code_graph_v1\",\n        \"tool\": \"get_file_impact\",\n        \"description\": \"Always check callers before patching an interface\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"verification_gate\": {\n      \"command\": \"npm test\",\n      \"required_exit_code\": 0,\n      \"max_retry_attempts\": 2\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n# 5. Why This Eliminates Both \"Too Much Code\" and \"Security Risks\"\n\n```\n┌──────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Dimension                            │ The Bloated Framework Approach       │ The AVOS Background Gadget Approach  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Developer Burden**                 │ Dev must write 1,500 lines of custom │ **Zero framework code.**             │\n│                                      │ AST tree parsers and execution loops.│ Dev creates a simple Gadget in 30s.  │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Security Boundary**                │ Dangerous: Custom code runs with     │ **Hardened: Gatekeepers.**           │\n│                                      │ full workspace access and raw keys.  │ Runs in an isolated V8 isolate with  │\n│                                      │                                      │ read-only access to files.           │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Domain Versatility**               │ Limited: Only works for code editors.│ **Universal: Works for code, finance,│\n│                                      │                                      │ legal, medical, and shipping.**      │\n├──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Agent Cognitive Load**             │ Confusing: AI must remember complex  │ **Dead simple: AI uses standard MCP**│\n│                                      │ multi-tier strategy commands.        │ tools like it was already trained on.│\n└──────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Summary of What This Establishes\n1. **Indexers \u0026 Graphers are Gadgets:** Whether parsing TypeScript ASTs, bank reconciliation ledgers, or legal statute citations, they live inside sandboxed **Cloudflare OS Gadgets** with private DO Facet SQLite databases.\n2. **Universal Interoperability via MCP v2:** The indexer automatically presents its data as `/mcp` tools (`find_impact`, `check_discrepancy`), which any agent can query instantly in 2ms.\n3. **Safe Declarative Pipelines:** Users and templates customize the agent\u0027s workflow by defining simple **Pre-flight hooks** and **Verification gates** in JSON, with zero dangerous execution scripts.",
