      }, {
        "text": " [Pass 2: Generate Diffs] ──► [Pass 3: Audit Diffs]\n     (1 Request)                 "
      }, {
        "text": "(1 Request)                 (1 Request)\n                                      ▲                           │\n                                      │ (If Audit Fails:"
      }, {
        "text": " Retry)   │ (If Approved)\n                                      └───────────────────────────┴──► [Git Commit]\n```\n\n####"
      }, {
        "text": " Request Breakdown Per Chunk:\n* **Happy Path (Passes on First Try):** **3 Requests** (Select"
      }, {
        "text": " $\\rightarrow$ Generate $\\rightarrow$ Review).\n* **1 Retry (Self-Healed):** **5 Requests** ($3 + 1"
      }, {
        "text": " \\text{ regenerate} + 1 \\text{ re-review}$).\n* **2 Retries (Self-Healed):** **7 Requests"
      }, {
        "text": "** ($3 + 2 \\text{ regenerations} + 2 \\text{ re-reviews}$).\n\n---"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\n### 3. How Much to Allow in the Loop? (The Hard Cap)\n\n\u003e **The Rule:"
      }, {
        "text": " Cap at Maximum 2 Retries (3 Total Generation Attempts).**\n\n#### Why you must never allow $\u003e2$ retries:\n1."
      }, {
        "text": " **The Hallucination Trap:** Empirical benchmarks show that if an LLM fails to correct code after 2 critique cycles"
      }, {
        "text": ", it enters a **circular failure loop** (fixing error A introduces error B, then fixing B brings back A).\n2. **Quota Preservation"
      }, {
        "text": ":** Without a hard cap, a single stubborn chunk with an obscure import bug could burn **40 requests in 5 minutes**, wiping"
      }, {
        "text": " out a chunk of your daily free budget.\n3. **Fallback Policy:** If attempt 3 fails the review:"
      }, {
        "text": "\n   * **Do not crash the Action.**\n   * Commit the code with a `"
      }, {
        "text": "[NEEDS_MANUAL_CHECK]` tag, save the reviewer\u0027s warning to `specs/phase-X/warnings.log`, and proceed"
      }, {
        "text": " to the next chunk so your cloud run finishes.\n\n---\n\n### 4. How Many Features Can You Build By End of Day?\n\nDepending on"
