      "text": "This approach provides a significant efficiency advantage. By analyzing your compressed codebase map **directly in this chat session once**, you eliminate Pass 1 (File Selection) from your GitHub Actions pipeline entirely.\n\nThis reduces your API consumption from **3 requests down to 2 requests per chunk** (a **33% reduction in API calls**), prevents rate-limit delays, and eliminates the risk of an automated model missing an important file during file selection.\n\n---\n\n### 1. How We Solve the \"Newly Created Files\" Problem\n\nWhen Chunk 1 creates a new file (for example, `packages/types/src/space-hierarchy.ts`), Chunk 2 and Chunk 3 will need to import and reference it.\n\nInstead of re-running a full `repomix --compress`, the runner script uses the **\"Branch Accumulator Pattern\"**:\n\n```\n[ Chunk 1: Reads existing SpaceDO.ts ]\n                 │\n                 ▼\n[ Chunk 1 creates `space-hierarchy.ts` \u0026 commits to branch ]\n                 │\n                 ▼\n[ Chunk 2 starts: ]\nBase Files (from spec): `workers/spaces/src/middleware/hierarchy.ts`\n        +\nAccumulated Branch Files (`git diff --name-only origin/main`): `space-hierarchy.ts`\n                 │\n                 ▼\n[ Targeted Repomix packs BOTH existing and newly created files! ]\n```\n\nBecause an entire phase only creates or touches 5 to 10 files total, automatically including **all files created or modified on the active branch so far** in subsequent chunks costs almost nothing in tokens (\u003c 1,500 tokens) and **guarantees that newly created types, classes, and DB schemas are immediately visible to later chunks.**\n\n---\n\n### 2. The Streamlined Chunk Spec Format\n\nEach chunk spec will have a simple `include_files:` header at the top:\n\n```markdown\n---\ninclude_files:\n  - workers/spaces/src/do/SpaceDO.ts\n  - packages/types/src/spaces.ts\nexpected_outputs:\n  - packages/types/src/space-hierarchy.ts\n---\n\n# Phase 1 - Chunk 01: Enterprise Depth Hierarch