      "text": "This distinction separates an **amateur AI agent playground** from an **enterprise-grade business operating system**.\n\nIf you treat all workflows the same, the system suffers from **Operational Blindness**:\n* A background CI/CD test failure in a dev project would alert the CEO on Telegram like a critical company emergency.\n* Conversely, a failure in the company’s nightly Stripe reconciliation pipeline would get lost in a dev chat thread.\n* The **Space Assistant (CEO)** would have no mental model of what is keeping the *business* alive versus what is simply a *vertical tool feature* of a single project.\n\nBy establishing a clean **3-Class Workflow Taxonomy**, every layer—the Space Assistant, the project agents, the billing engine, and the human founder—knows the exact **scope, authority, budget, and escalation path** of every running process.\n\n---\n\n# 1. The 3-Class Workflow Taxonomy\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                   THE 3-CLASS WORKFLOW TAXONOMY                                        │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 🏢 CLASS 1: COMPANY AUTOMATIONS (The Business Nervous System)                                          │\n│ • Scope: Space-Wide (Root Company Level)                                                               │\n│ • Owner: Space Assistant (\"The CEO\") / Business Operations                                             │\n│ • Purpose: Core business processes that replace Zapier, Make, and backend servers.                     │\n│ • Examples: Nightly Stripe reconciliation, lead triage, partner payouts, SLA monitors.                 │\n│ • Escalation: Alerts the Founder / Managing Partner immediately via Telegram/WhatsApp.                 │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ ⚙️ CLASS 2: VERTICAL EXTENSION WORKFLOWS (The Plugin Domain Engine)                                     │\n│ • Scope: Project-Bound (Tied to 1 Project Kind or Installed Plugin)                                    │\n│ • Owner: Project Domain Engine / Bundled in `plugin.json`                                              │\n│ • Purpose: Makes the project operate like a dedicated vertical platform (Cursor, Harvey, Hebbia).     │\n│ • Examples: Continuous CI/CD test runner on Git push, background AST code graph indexer,               │\n│             bulk contract ETL data room parser, weekly municipal zoning scraper.                       │\n│ • Escalation: Posts to the Project Team Room (Tier 1) or updates a Pull Request card.                  │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ ⚡ CLASS 3: EPHEMERAL TASK WORKFLOWS (The Agent On-Demand Sagas)                                        │\n│ • Scope: Task-Bound (Tied to 1 specific Task DAG node in the Project Journal)                          │\n│ • Owner: Individual Functional Agent (e.g. `@DevOperator` or `@GrowthOperator`)                       │\n│ • Purpose: Heavy on-demand execution that exceeds HTTP timeouts or needs dormant sleeps/retries.       │\n│ • Examples: Two-pass Repomix chunk implementation, 50-page web crawl, video-to-skill learning.         │\n│ • Escalation: Reports back to the calling agent; posts an inline Receipt Card in the active thread.    │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 2. Comprehensive Comparison Matrix\n\n```\n┌───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Operational Dimension         │ Class 1: Company Automations  │ Class 2: Vertical Extensions  │ Class 3: Ephemeral Tasks        │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Where It Lives**            │ `spaces/:id/automations/`     │ `/.avos/shared/workflows/`    │ `/.avos/tasks/:taskId/`         │\n│                               │ (Root SpaceDO Registry)       │ (Bundled in `plugin.json`)    │ (Dynamically generated by agent)│\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Trigger Origin**            │ Crons (`0 8 * * *`),          │ Project events (`git_push`,   │ On-demand agent tool call       │\n│                               │ Webhooks (Stripe, Whop)       │ `file_saved`, Parse 5 upload) │ (`ctx.workflows.start(...)`)    │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **AI Involvement**            │ **Mostly Deterministic (95%)**│ **Hybrid Deterministic (80%)**│ **AI-Heavy (70%)**              │\n│                               │ Pure code; AI for anomalies   │ Code + domain linters/ASTs    │ Reasoning turns + CodeAct edits │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Failure Escalation Path**   │ **Direct to Founder:**        │ **Direct to Project Room:**   │ **Direct to Origin Thread:**    │\n│                               │ Telegram/WhatsApp alert       │ PR card or Team Room issue    │ 2-line expandable Receipt Card  │\n├───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────┤\n│ **Billing \u0026 Spend Source**    │ Company Master Operating      │ Project Local Spend Cap       │ Active Task / User Credit       │\n│                               │ Wallet (`SpaceDO.wallet`)     │ (Defined per Sub-Space)       │ Allowance (1,200 plan credits)  │\n└───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n# 3. How the Space Assistant (CEO) Uses This Distinction\n\nBecause workflows declare their operational class, the **Space Assistant** knows how to behave without confusing noise:\n\n```\n                                  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n                                  │         SPACE ASSISTANT (\"The CEO\")          │\n                                  │   Standing Morning Audit (08:00 UTC)         │\n                                  └──────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘\n                                                         │\n                         ┌───────────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────┐\n                         ▼                               ▼                               ▼\n┌──────────────────────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────────────────────┐   ┌──────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. REVIEWS COMPANY AUTOMATIONS   │   │ 2. INSPECTS VERTICAL EXTENSIONS  │   │ 3. IGNORES EPHEMERAL TASKS       │\n├──────────────────────────────────┤   ├──────────────────────────────────┤   ├──────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Evaluates business vitals:       │   │ Checks if projects are stalled:  │   │ Does NOT review individual       │\n│ • Stripe reconciliation: Verified│   │ • Did the CI/CD pipeline fail?   │   │ file scrapes or short-lived      │\n│ • Net cash flow: +$1,420 (24h)   │   │ • Is the code indexer running?   │   │ Repomix chunk runs (they belong  │\n│ • Lead SLA response time: 3.2m   │   │ • Only steps in if a project has │   │ strictly to the project agent\u0027s  │\n│ ➡️ Compiles Morning Founder Brief │   │   been blocked for \u003e 24 hours.   │   │ internal task DAG).              │\n└──────────────────────────────────┘   └──────────────────────────────────┘   └──────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### Scenario A: A Class 1 Company Automation Fails\n* **What happens:** The nightly Stripe reconciliation workflow hits a bank discrepancy of $450.\n* **Space Assistant Action:** It classifies this as a **Critical Business Anomaly**. It does not post in a developer chat; it immediately pings the founder\u0027s paired Telegram:\n  \u003e *\"⚠️ Financial Alert: Nightly bank reconciliation found a $450 discrepancy in Stripe invoice #8492. [Review Ledger] [Approve Adjustment]\"*\n\n### Scenario B: A Class 2 Vertical Extension Workflow Fails\n* **What happens:** The `ContinuousIntegrationWorkflow` runs `npm test` on `branch:feature-darkmode` and fails 2 unit tests.\n* **Space Assistant Action:** It stays silent. The failure is **local to the project**.\n* **Project Action:** The workflow updates the active Pull Request card in the **Tier 1 Team Room**:\n  \u003e *\"❌ PR #14 Build Failed: 2 tests failed in `src/Header.test.ts`. @DevOperator has been assigned to investigate.\"*\n\n---\n\n# 4. Declarative Schema: `workflow.json` / `SpaceDO` Registry\n\nIn `packages/types/src/workflow.ts`, every workflow registers its classification:\n\n```typescript\nexport interface AvosWorkflowDefinition {\n  id: string; // e.g. \"stripe_daily_reconciler\"\n  name: string;\n  description: string;\n\n  // ── THE TAXONOMY SWITCH ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  workflowClass: \"COMPANY_AUTOMATION\" | \"VERTICAL_EXTENSION\" | \"EPHEMERAL_TASK\";\n\n  // ── SCOPING \u0026 OWNERSHIP ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  scope: \"SPACE_WIDE\" | \"PROJECT_BOUND\" | \"TASK_BOUND\";\n  spaceId: string;\n  projectId?: string; // Optional if space-wide\n  bundledByPluginId?: string; // e.g. \"plugin_edge_ide_v1\"\n\n  // ── TRIGGER \u0026 LIFECYCLE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n  trigger: {\n    type: \"cron\" | \"webhook\" | \"event_queue\" | \"on_demand\";\n    cronExpression?: string;  // e.g. \"0 8 * * *\"\n    eventTopic?: string;      // e.g. \"git.branch_pushed\", \"stripe.charge_dispute\"\n  };\n\n  // ── GOVERNANCE \u0026 SAFETY CEILINGS ─────────────────────────────────────────\n  governance: {\n    maxStepCeiling: number;        // e.g. 50 steps\n    stepTimeoutSeconds: number;    // e.g. 300s (5 minutes)\n    alertChannel: \"FOUNDER_TELEGRAM\" | \"PROJECT_TEAM_ROOM\" | \"THREAD_RECEIPT_ONLY\";\n    fundingSource: \"COMPANY_WALLET\" | \"PROJECT_CAP\" | \"USER_CREDITS\";\n  };\n\n  // ── SCRIPT HARNESS ENTRYPOINT ─────────────────────────────────────────────\n  entrypointPath: string; // e.g. \"./workflows/reconcile.ts\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### Database Schema in `SpaceDO.ts` SQLite\n\nTrack all workflows centrally so both the Space Assistant and project agents have full observability:\n\n```sql\n-- Central Workflows Registry (SpaceDO SQLite)\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS space_workflows_registry (\n  id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,                       -- e.g. \"wf_stripe_reconcile_01\"\n  space_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  project_id TEXT,                           -- NULL for Company Automations\n  workflow_class TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (workflow_class IN (\u0027COMPANY_AUTOMATION\u0027, \u0027VERTICAL_EXTENSION\u0027, \u0027EPHEMERAL_TASK\u0027)),\n  title TEXT NOT NULL,\n  plugin_id TEXT,                            -- Links to owning plugin if vertical extension\n  trigger_type TEXT NOT NULL,                -- \u0027cron\u0027, \u0027webhook\u0027, \u0027event\u0027, \u0027on_demand\u0027\n  trigger_spec TEXT,                         -- \"0 8 * * *\" or \"stripe.charge.failed\"\n  funding_source TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT \u0027PROJECT_CAP\u0027,\n  alert_channel TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT \u0027PROJECT_TEAM_ROOM\u0027,\n  status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT \u0027ACTIVE\u0027 CHECK (status IN (\u0027ACTIVE\u0027, \u0027PAUSED\u0027, \u0027DISABLED\u0027)),\n  last_run_at TEXT,\n  last_exit_code INTEGER,\n  created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT (datetime(\u0027now\u0027))\n);\n```\n\n---\n\n# 5. Summary of Why This Completes the Architecture\n\n1. **Eliminates Alert Fatigue:** The founder only gets alerted for real **Company Automations** (money, legal, churn). Routine development or research workflows stay contained in their project workstations.\n2. **True Vertical Customization:** A plugin author can package a complete software product by bundling **Class 2 Vertical Extensions** (e.g., CI/CD runners, AST graphers, customs dockets) that run automatically in that project without confusing the rest of the company.\n3. **Clean Budget Accounting:** Compute is billed to the right balance: Company Automations draw from the master company wallet, Vertical Extensions draw from the sub-space department budget, and Ephemeral Tasks draw from the user\u0027s active credit pack.\n4. **Architectural Coherence:** The Space Assistant now has an **executive operational map** of the business, knowing at any second which background workflows are keeping the company alive versus which ones are just internal tooling.",
