re.\n\n\n**Implementing Access Control**\n\nI\u0027m now designing fine-grained RBAC for connectors in Dynamic Workflows. I\u0027m focusing on a Gatekeeper layer using Cloudflare Workers to enforce ACL policies assigned to connectors in `SpaceDO`. This will involve intercepting tool calls to validate permissions before they reach Composio, ensuring secure and controlled access based on defined roles and allowed/denied actions, such as preventing email sending based on a user\u0027s role.\n\n\n**Addressing Scope and Idempotency**\n\nI\u0027m now grappling with \"Silent Disconnect\" issues from scope mismatches and addressing idempotency. The plan: implement scope-aware pre-flight validation and incremental re-authentication. I\u0027m also planning to tackle the risk of duplicate executions from webhook replay storms. I\u0027ll need to define a solution that considers the failure modes of Zapier and Make, to create autonomous AI robustness.\n\n\n**Tackling Common Automation Failures**\n\nI\u0027m now zeroing in on failure scenarios, specifically duplicated actions due to network retries, and designing solutions. I\u0027m focusing on the *idempotency-key* to prevent repeated emails or charges from automated retries. I\u0027m also addressing the infinite self-triggering loops with a global event counter and origin attribution. Then, I am focusing on schema drift with runtime JSON schema validation and an LLM-powered repair mechanism.\n\n\n**Clarifying Account Routing**\n\nI\u0027m now prioritizing scenarios with multiple connected accounts, such as choosing between `support@`, `billing@`, and `ceo@` when sending an email. My plan is to add explicit connection tagging, enabling alias routing, for example: `ctx.connectors.gmail.using(\"support@\")`.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Protecting Sensitive Data**\n\nI\u0027m also tackling data security, particularly the risk of accidental PII leakage. The strategy is to integrate Egress DLP filters into Outbound Workers. These filters will scan outgoing payloads for sensitive information like credit card numbers, SSNs, and private tokens before data leaves the system.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Managing Unattended Authentication**\n\nFinally, I\u0027m focusing on unattended authentication flows. I\u0027m focusing on solving the issue where background jobs requiring missing connections can\u0027t show a popup. The workflow will pause into a `PENDING_AUTH` state and trigger a notification.\n\n\n",
