ts \u0026 Stateful Gadgets│ 7 Studio Kinds, Background Indexers, DO Facets  │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 7 │ Asymmetric Workflows, Queues \u0026 Telephony   │ Inbound Webhooks, Queues, Replay Lake, Voice    │\n├─────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ Phase 8 │ Billing, Marketplace, Distribution \u0026 Shell │ Credits, Subscriptions, Trigger Recipes, Radar  │\n└─────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 1: Multi-Tenant Core, Storage \u0026 Workspace Foundation (Items 1–7)\n*Prerequisite: Clean repository. Bedrock database, multi-tenancy, and filesystem layer.*\n\n1. **Enterprise Depth Hierarchy:** Parent Company Space (Depth 0) $\\rightarrow$ Department Sub-Spaces (Depth 1) in D1 schema.\n2. **Sub-Space Inheritance \u0026 Isolation Matrix:** Downward admin oversight, strict upward isolation, and zero lateral bleed without capability grants.\n3. **Public vs. Private Project Access Control:** In-DO SQLite project visibility (`public` vs `private`) and membership ACL verification.\n4. **Project-Anchored Automation Architecture:** Company automations live inside dedicated, versioned projects (e.g., `Project: Treasury`) rather than unmanaged root scripts.\n5. **Cloudflare Artifacts Git-for-Agents Engine:** Zig-to-WASM Git server running in Durable Objects for 10ms micro-forks, branch tracking, and commit trees.\n6. **`@cloudflare/computer` In-Memory Virtual POSIX Shell:** `just-bash` parser executing POSIX commands against DO SQLite `workspace_files`.\n7. **Clean Namespace Separation:** Strict boundary isolation between `/workspace/` (user application code) and `/.avos/` (internal agent state, skills, and memory).\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 2: Compute Ladder \u0026 Invisible Runtime Hypervisor (Items 8–19)\n*Prerequisite: Phase 1 (Requires the SQLite VFS and Git Artifacts engine).*\n\n8. **6-Tier Cloudflare Execution Ladder:** Dynamic escalation routing (T1 Virtual FS $\\rightarrow$ T2 Isolates $\\rightarrow$ T3 Workflows $\\rightarrow$ T4 Kitesurf $\\rightarrow$ T5 Chromium $\\rightarrow$ T6 Containers).\n9. **Invisible Runtime Hypervisor:** Minimalist tool surface (`Bash`, `Read`, `Edit`, `Browser`, `Delegate`) routing transparently underneath `Bash`.\n10. **`ArtifactFS` FUSE Driver with Lazy Hydration:** Mounts project repository files into Linux Containers on demand in 5ms.\n11. **4-Dimension State Synchronization Engine:** Bidirectional sync across Filesystem, Shell CWD/Env, Git HEAD, and SQLite DB state.\n12. **95/5 Compute Arbitrage with 60-Second Micro-Sleep:** Sub-5ms V8 Isolate execution for 95% of tasks + 60-second container micro-sleep countdown.\n13. **In-Isolate WebAssembly Python (Pyodide):** Lightweight Python runs in V8 in \u003c10ms for $0.00; auto-elevates to Tier 6 only for native C-extensions.\n14. **Tier 4 Cloudflare Kitesurf Agent Browser:** 30MB low-memory DOM extraction with transparent Tier 5 Chromium fallback for WebGL/screenshots.\n15. **Virtual Display Container Automation (\"Computer Use\"):** Xvfb + Fluxbox + noVNC WebSockets for desktop GUI automation.\n16. **Multiplexed Persistent gRPC Bridge:** Sub-5ms binary communication between Durable Objects and Containers over persistent TCP sockets.\n17. **Instant Zero-Copy Branch Micro-Forking:** Programmatic 10ms repository forks for subagents, tasks, and private scratchpads.\n18. **Turn-by-Turn Git Time Machine:** Automatic commit generation per tool turn with 1-click historical rollback in the thread timeline.\n19. **Reasoning-Aware Git Blame:** Front-matter commit attribution storing the technical and legal rationale behind every code change.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 3: Action Space, Virtual CLI \u0026 Decoupled Auth (Items 20–38)\n*Prerequisite: Phase 2 (Requires execution primitives and hypervisor router).*\n\n20. **Universal Runtime SDK (`ctx`):** Typed API exposed to scripts (`fs`, `project`, `space`, `vault`, `cli`, `browser`, `connectors`).\n21. **Universal Vault Layer with Edge Outbound Workers:** Zero-leak secret injection at the edge network boundary.\n22. **WriteGuard Mutation Interceptor:** Edge proxy SQL AST and destructive tool filter blocking unauthorized mutations.\n23. **Virtual CLI Interception Engine:** Translates CLI commands (`stripe`, `gh`, `r2`, `jq`) into edge REST/Wasm calls in \u003c5ms.\n24. **Just-In-Time (JIT) Virtual CLI Synthesis:** Agent micro-synthesizes missing CLI commands on-the-fly using `ctx.cli.register` and `ctx.cli.extend`.\n25. **Decoupled Logical Connector Binding Matrix (`project_connector_bindings`):** Maps logical aliases (e.g. `inbound_mail`) to physical connections without hardcoding account names in code.\n26. **Pre-Flight Scope Verification \u0026 Incremental Re-Auth:** Detects scope mismatches before execution; emits an MCP-UI scope upgrade card.\n27. **Gatekeeper Capability-Based Cross-Subspace Delegation:** Cryptographically signed, attenuated resource grants between departments.\n28. **3-Tier Connector Scoping:** Space-Shared, Project-Bound, and User-Personal credential separation.\n29. **Public Channel Tool Stripping \u0026 MCP-UI Privacy Bridge:** Strips personal tools in public rooms; forks to private scratchpads via interactive card.\n30. **Single-Use Ephemeral Action Grants:** In-channel 15-second capability signing via MCP v2 Elicitation cards.\n31. **Turn-Holder vs. Referent Mention Router:** First `@mention` receives the turn lock; subsequent mentions become context references.\n32. **Sequential Turn Delegation (`ctx.agent.delegate`):** Orderly handoffs between agents preventing multi-agent collision.\n33. **Cryptographic Delegation Chaining:** Task token carries the initiating human user\u0027s ID and role rank, preventing privilege escalation.\n34. **Demonstration-to-Skill Distillation Engine:** Execution traces parameterize into reusable TypeScript skills in `/.avos/shared/skills/`.\n35. **Multimodal Video-to-Skill Learning Engine:** Screen recordings (Whisper audio + Vision keyframes) synthesize into parameterized skills.\n36. **Zero-Turn Tool Catalog in Prompt:** Injects available CLI index into system prompt; implementation code loaded only on demand.\n37. **Declarative Step Pipelines (Execution Hooks):** Pre-flight context hooks (`pre_flight_mcp`) and verification gates configured via JSON.\n38. **Egress Data Loss Prevention (PII Scrubber):** Scans outgoing payloads to public connectors (Discord, Instagram, X) for sensitive data.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 4: Cognition, Memory, Knowledge \u0026 Ingestion (Items 39–53)\n*Prerequisite: Phase 3 (Requires security boundaries, Vault, and SDK tools).*\n\n39. **Universal Agent Execution Kernel (`NaelaoAgentDO`):** Single unified REPL engine powering all functional roles.\n40. **Dynamic 4-Layer System Prompt Assembly:** Universal Kernel $\\rightarrow$ Business Identity $\\rightarrow$ `SOUL.md` $\\rightarrow$ Founder Directives.\n41. **Hardware-Enforced Role Firewalls (`AgentFirewall`):** Physical schema stripping based on declared functional role.\n42. **Dual-Tier Planner-Worker Asymmetry Engine:** `/goal` command creates a clean Task DAG; anonymous workers execute code.\n43. **3-Layer Hybrid Memory Architecture:** Active Turn RAM $\\rightarrow$ Deterministic `PROJECT.md` $\\rightarrow$ Vectorize Long-Term Semantic.\n44. **Cross-Thread Context Isolation:** Pristine context per thread; historical raw chat logs are never carried over.\n45. **Semantic Fact Gating (Hindsight Memory):** Learnings distilled into atomic rules; retrieved only if cosine similarity is $\u003e0.80$.\n46. **In-Flight Milestone Squashing (`compact_context`):** Archives older message history to D1 while preserving active task state.\n47. **Jack Dorsey Mini-AGI Sovereign Permission Model:** Decentralized, role-clamped intelligence per employee.\n48. **Hardware-Level Vector Pre-Filtering:** Integer role ranks (1–5) and bitmasks evaluated directly inside Cloudflare Vectorize.\n49. **Mathematical Bitmask Evaluation \u0026 XML Envelopes:** Wraps dynamic retrieval chunks in `\u003ccontext_chunk\u003e` untrusted boundary tags.\n50. **Cohere Parse 5 (`parse-v5.0`) Edge Ingestion Pipeline:** Converts enterprise PDFs, faxes, and complex tables into clean Markdown.\n51. **Google Search AI Mode at the Edge:** Sub-50ms KV semantic caching + Dense/Sparse Hybrid Reciprocal Rank Fusion ($k\u003d60$).\n52. **Interactive Numbered Citation Footnotes:** Markdown stream anchored directly to verified chunk coordinates in R2.\n53. **Inter-Project Stateless MCP v2 Mesh:** Every project exposes `/mcp` via `createMcpHandler` over Streamable HTTP (Composio as OAuth broker).\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 5: 4-Tier Threads \u0026 Multi-Assistant Governance (Items 54–75)\n*Prerequisite: Phase 4 (Requires agent kernel, memory boundaries, and Git mesh).*\n\n54. **4-Tier Thread Hierarchy:** Team Rooms (Tier 1), Task Workstations (Tier 2), Consult Lanes (Tier 3), Private Scratchpads (Tier 4).\n55. **Solo 2-Tier Cockpit vs. Multi-User 4-Tier Digital Office:** Dynamic elevation when a teammate is invited.\n56. **Optimistic Concurrency Control (OCC):** Atomic Compare-And-Swap file writes verified against SHA-256 base hashes.\n57. **Distributed File-Level Mutex Locks:** 30-second TTL locks in `ConcurrencyDO` for multi-file refactoring runs.\n58. **Inline Pull Request (PR) Review Cards:** Interactive visual AST diff cards with 1-click fast-forward merges.\n59. **Upstream Staleness Detection \u0026 Auto-Rebase:** Real-time divergence detection and automated conflict-free rebasing.\n60. **Atomic Task Lease Protocol (`SpaceDO.tasks` CAS):** Single-writer leases with 15-min crash-proof TTL preventing duplicate work.\n61. **Sibling Assistant Spectator \u0026 Review Mode:** Non-claiming assistants observe, avoid duplicate execution, and offer PR audits.\n62. **Semantic Intent Deduplication Gat