      "text": "**Revising Bot Architecture**\n\nI\u0027m currently focused on the underlying architecture for customer-facing bot projects. I\u0027m exploring how to best redefine this architecture, specifically considering bots classified as \"customer_bot\" to ensure they are most effectively structured. This is the central problem I am now working on.\n\n\n**Clarifying Customer Interactions**\n\nI\u0027ve clarified the separation between the main project agent and customer-facing bots. It\u0027s now apparent that the main agent acts as an orchestrator, while custom background Dynamic Workflows, subagents, or automations handle external user interactions across platforms like WhatsApp or Discord. These subagents utilize the `ctx` for message handling and data persistence within the project\u0027s ecosystem.\n\n\n**Developing Bot Modules**\n\nNow I\u0027m focusing on modularizing the approach to customer-facing bot design. I\u0027m exploring prebuilt subagents and automations for a marketplace, enabling developers to build and sell \"recipes\" for `customer_bot` projects. The system would also let users prompt the agent to synthesize these, such as creating a Shopify returns bot. Security remains a core consideration, ensuring these subagents have scoped permissions and zero access to the project\u0027s core components.\n\n\n**Defining Bot Interaction Planes**\n\nI\u0027m now detailing the system\u0027s interaction layers. Layer 1 involves users interacting with the main Project Agent via a defined interface, such as \"Build an intake automation for dental appointments on WhatsApp.\" Layer 2 defines how external user messages flow to the Customer Service Subagent, through validation, queueing, and dispatch, within the `CustomerBotContext`. I\u0027m focused on ensuring these interactions are secure and efficient.\n\n\n**Analyzing Bot Telemetry**\n\nI\u0027m now integrating telemetry and analytics. Each bot conversation turn will log to SQLite, specifically the `project_customer_conversations` and `customer_messages` tables. I\u0027ll then have the main Agent periodically analyze these logs to summarize common complaints, identify feature requests/bugs (which it\u0027ll log to the project journal), and escalate urgent issues to the Executive Copilot. I am also working on recipes for the marketplace, specifically `recipe_dental_whatsapp_receptionist`, `recipe_shopify_returns_bot`, and `recipe_discord_support_triage`. Developers will package these, and buyers can install.\n\n\n**Defining Bot Deployment**\n\nI\u0027m now detailing the deployment process. Users will bind their accounts via Composio with a single click. This architecture resolves customer bot security hazards by using a quarantined, lightweight subagent. I\u0027m focusing on a dual-plane architecture: a Management Plane (User to Project Agent) and a Customer Ingress Plane (Public Customers to Dynamic Workflow Subagent). The `CustomerBotContext` will limit access to core functionality.\n\n\n",
