rns, completed decisions squash into `PROJECT.md`, older turns archive to D1, and the prompt retains only the summary plus recent turns.\n* **Invariants:** Active task state is preserved verbatim; conversational small talk is pruned.\n\n#### 47. Jack Dorsey Mini-AGI Sovereign Permission Model\n* **Mental Model:** Intelligence is decentralized and partitioned to the individual user rather than an all-seeing black box.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Every employee’s assistant operates with clearance clamped to that employee\u0027s role rank.\n* **Invariants:** An assistant cannot perceive, summarize, or retrieve documents the human is not cleared to see.\n\n#### 48. Hardware-Level Vector Pre-Filtering\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents information leakage through vector search ranking density.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Filters metadata (space ID, project ID, role rank) inside Cloudflare Vectorize *before* similarity scoring.\n* **Invariants:** Unauthorized document chunks are physically discarded prior to nearest-neighbor thresholding.\n\n#### 49. Mathematical Bitmask Evaluation \u0026 XML Envelopes\n* **Mental Model:** Defense-in-depth against prompt injection from retrieved documents.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Evaluates bitwise permissions ($\\mathbf{m}_i \\wedge \\mathbf{u} \\neq \\mathbf{0}$) and wraps chunks in `\u003ccontext_chunk\u003e` semantic boundary tags.\n* **Invariants:** Text within context tags cannot alter system instructions or tool policies.\n\n#### 50. Cohere Parse 5 (`parse-v5.0`) Edge Ingestion Pipeline\n* **Mental Model:** The missing ingestion layer for vertical AI startups. Replaces fragile OCR with a 2.3B Vision Model.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Converts scanned leases, faxes, accident reports, and financial tables into clean Markdown at the edge.\n* **Invariants:** Preserves multi-column layout structures, headers, and footnotes without text garbling.\n\n#### 51. Google Search AI Mode at the Edge\n* **Mental Model:** Delivers Google-Search-grade speed, precision, and grounding at Cloudflare\u0027s edge.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Sub-50ms KV semantic cache + Dense/Sparse Hybrid Reciprocal Rank Fusion ($k\u003d60$) combining Vectorize and BM25.\n* **Invariants:** Queries with cosine similarity \u003e0.96 return cached answers in 35ms with zero LLM generation cost.\n\n#### 52. Interactive Numbered Citation Footnotes\n* **Mental Model:** Verifiable answers for legal, financial, and medical compliance.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Streams text with clickable citation badges (`[1]`, `[2]`) anchored to specific chunk coordinates in R2.\n* **Invariants:** Every factual claim in vertical cowork mode must cite an authoritative document coordinate.\n\n#### 53. Inter-Project Stateless MCP v2 Mesh\n* **Mental Model:** Transforms the entire company into a self-discovering microservice mesh.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Every project exposes a stateless `/mcp` endpoint via Cloudflare MCP SDK v2 over Streamable HTTP.\n* **Invariants:** Projects communicate over standardized tool calls without open SSE sockets or custom RPC glue.\n\n#### 54. Composio Managed SaaS OAuth Broker Integration\n* **Mental Model:** Zero-friction enterprise authentication for 500+ third-party tools.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Composio handles hosted OAuth flows and token refreshes. Pipedream is completely dropped to eliminate duplicate bloat.\n* **Invariants:** Tools are fetched Just-In-Time; raw API keys are never managed manually by users.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 5: 4-Tier Threads \u0026 Multi-Assistant Governance\n\n#### 55. 4-Tier Thread Hierarchy\n* **Mental Model:** Eliminates thread sprawl and uncoordinated chatter across teams.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Enforces 4 thread kinds: Team Rooms (Tier 1), Task Workstations (Tier 2), Consult Lanes (Tier 3), and Private Scratchpads (Tier 4).\n* **Invariants:** Every thread enforces distinct visibility and write permissions.\n\n#### 56. Solo 2-Tier Cockpit vs. Multi-User 4-Tier Digital Office\n* **Mental Model:** Adapts UI complexity based on team size.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Solo users get a streamlined 2-Tier Cockpit (Chat + Live Canvas). Inviting a teammate dynamically unlocks the full 4-Tier Digital Office.\n* **Invariants:** Solo workflows experience zero collaboration bureaucracy; team projects enforce PR review cards.\n\n#### 57. Optimistic Concurrency Control (OCC) with SHA-256 Checkpoints\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents concurrent users or agents from silently overwriting each other\u0027s code.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** SQLite file updates enforce conditional writes verified against the base content hash.\n* **Invariants:** If another thread modified the file mid-turn, the transaction aborts with fresh line hints.\n\n#### 58. Distributed File-Level Mutex Locks (`ConcurrencyDO`)\n* **Mental Model:** Coordinates complex multi-file refactoring operations safely.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Agents acquire 30-second TTL locks on specific file keys.\n* **Invariants:** Crashed agents automatically release locks upon TTL expiration, preventing permanent deadlocks.\n\n#### 59. Inline Pull Request (PR) Review Cards\n* **Mental Model:** Code reviews happen naturally inside the chat timeline.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Merges from branches to `main` render interactive cards with visual AST diffs, author attribution, and one-click fast-forward merge buttons.\n* **Invariants:** Direct unreviewed commits to `main` are blocked in multi-user team projects.\n\n#### 60. Upstream Staleness Detection \u0026 Auto-Rebase\n* **Mental Model:** Keeps active working branches synchronized with master development.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Detects when a branch is behind `main`. Autonomously rebases non-conflicting files and flags overlaps for review.\n* **Invariants:** Branches display real-time divergence badges (`2 commits behind main`).\n\n#### 61. Atomic Task Lease Protocol (`SpaceDO.tasks` CAS)\n* **Mental Model:** Eliminates duplicate work and wasted credits when an incident occurs.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Sibling assistants attempt an atomic compare-and-swap write in SQLite. Exactly one assistant wins the 15-minute lease; others abort immediately.\n* **Invariants:** Zero duplicate LLM generation turns on shared project bugs.\n\n#### 62. Sibling Assistant Spectator \u0026 Review Mode\n* **Mental Model:** Non-claiming assistants remain helpful without generating conflicting code.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Sibling assistants observe active tasks, update their users\u0027 notification feeds, and offer to audit incoming PR diffs.\n* **Invariants:** Spectator assistants never fork competing branches for an active task lease.\n\n#### 63. Semantic Intent Deduplication Gate\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents two humans from accidentally ordering the same feature twice.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Embeds incoming prompts and checks active tasks for \u003e0.85 cosine similarity. Intercepts duplicates and offers to join the existing thread.\n* **Invariants:** Prevents conflicting duplicate branches before code generation begins.\n\n#### 64. Sponsor Alignment Gate (RFC Trigger)\n* **Mental Model:** Protects projects from contradictory architectural orders from different owners.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** If two assistants issue opposing commands on core architecture (e.g. auth providers), the project agent freezes execution and posts an RFC discussion card.\n* **Invariants:** Code modifications halt until human consensus or admin approval is recorded.\n\n#### 65. 2-Round Deliberation Horizon\n* **Mental Model:** Halts runaway bot-to-bot gossip loops.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Limits autonomous agent debate to 2 rounds. If consensus is not reached, transitions to `BLOCKED_AWAITING_HUMAN`.\n* **Invariants:** Prevents infinite LLM ping-pong loops while humans sleep.\n\n#### 66. Single On-Call Alert Routing\n* **Mental Model:** Eliminates notification cascades and the bystander effect.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Project failures alert only the designated project lead\u0027s assistant rather than broadcasting to all team members.\n* **Invariants:** Exactly one human is assigned primary ownership of an operational alert.\n\n#### 67. Immutable Cryptographic Provenance Ledger (`provenance_ledger`)\n* **Mental Model:** Non-repudiation and regulatory auditability (SOC2/HIPAA).\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Records a 4-point cryptographic audit trail linking Human Trigger $\\rightarrow$ Assistant Actor $\\rightarrow$ Project Executor $\\rightarrow$ Git Commit Hash.\n* **Invariants:** Every change can be legally traced back to human authorization.\n\n#### 68. Multi-Branch Parallel Model Benchmarking Races\n* **Mental Model:** Finds the best solution for hard coding puzzles through competition.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Forks 3 isolated branches for 3 models in parallel. Evaluates test assertions and merges the winning implementation.\n* **Invariants:** Failed implementations are discarded without touching the main branch.\n\n#### 69. Real-Time Multiplayer Presence via `WsHubDO`\n* **Mental Model:** Real-time awareness across teams like Figma or Google Docs.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** WebSockets broadcast live file editing presence and cursor states to all connected clients.\n* **Invariants:** Stale connections are aged out automatically after 90 seconds of silence.\n\n#### 70. Invoker-Attested Split-Actor Model\n* **Mental Model:** Solves the persona paradox in multi-user channels.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Private scratchpads spawn personal actor instances with private memory; public channels spawn canonical actors with shared memory.\n* **Invariants:** Personal notes never bleed into public channel responses.\n\n#### 71. Vertical-Scoped Certified Model Whitelist (`whitelist_only`)\n* **Mental Model:** Guarantees compliance in regulated healthcare, legal, and finance spaces.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Server-side validation rejecting any model not certified for that space template.\n* **Invariants:** Unapproved community or loose conversational models are blocked at the router layer.\n\n#### 72. Private LoRA Model Dynamic Edge Loading\n* **Mental Model:** Seamless access to proprietary enterprise models.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Routes `custom/*` model calls through Cloudflare AI Gateway, dynamically injecting LoRA adapter weights onto base models at edge runtime.\n* **Invariants:** Custom models appear automatically at the top of the team\u0027s Model Selector.\n\n#### 73. Sovereign Enterprise Air-Gapped Local AI Engine\n* **Mental Model:** Zero data egress for defense, healthcare, and banking clients.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Connects to on-premise GPU clusters running Ollama / vLLM via `LocalTunnelDO` over encrypted outbound WebSockets.\n* **Invariants:** 100% of prompt and document bytes execute locally on client hardware.\n\n#### 74. Strict Air-Gapped Space Compliance Lock\n* **Mental Model:** Physical enforcement of data sovereignty.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Router-level block preventing any request from reaching external cloud AI APIs when compliance lock is engaged.\n* **Invariants:** System halts safely with an alert rather than failing over to cloud endpoints.\n\n#### 75. Finite Task Project Auto-Sleep\n* **Mental Model:** Zero idle compute bills on completed projects.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** When the Project Journal DAG hits 100% completion, Durable Objects clear all alarms and hibernate at $0 cost.\n* **Invariants:** Finite projects wake up only when a human sends a new message.\n\n#### 76. Progressive Disclosure Interface (\"Apple Surface, Linux Edge\")\n* **Mental Model:** Consumer simplicity on the surface, full enterprise power underneath.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Defaults to Business Mode (plain English cards, live previews). Power users can opt into Developer Mode (Git commit trees, raw terminal logs).\n* **Invariants:** Non-technical users are never exposed to raw Git conflicts or infrastructure tiers.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 6: Project Kinds, Viewports, Extensions \u0026 Durable Daemons\n\n#### 77. Dual-Mode Operating System\n* **Mental Model:** Seamless switching between autonomous company building and collaborative consulting desks.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Defined via `template_mode` in `blueprint.json`: toggles between autonomous operator pipelines and human-in-the-loop cowork studios.\n* **Invariants:** Determines default autonomy postures, channel roles, and central viewport layouts.\n\n#### 78. Canvas-First / Domain Viewport Architecture\n* **Mental Model:** The workspace canvas is the primary product; chat is secondary.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Center viewport mounts specialized canvases: code editors, contract redliners, spreadsheet formula grids, or live web previews.\n* **Invariants:** Canvas viewports hot-reload workspace file changes live over WebSockets in sub-150ms.\n\n#### 79. The 7 Foundational Project Kinds\n* **Mental Model:** The foundational workspace types powering any business venture.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Standardized implementations: `product_dev`, `doc_studio`, `voice_agent`, `customer_bot`, `model_studio`, `growth_engine`, `app_studio`.\n* **Invariants:** Every project must declare a valid kind defining its allowed compute ladder tiers and lifecycle.\n\n#### 80. Cloudflare OS Stateful Gadgets\n* **Mental Model:** Living full-stack micro-applications built from prompts in 30 seconds.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Runs inside sandboxed Dynamic Worker isolates backed by dedicated DO Facet SQLite databases.\n* **Invariants:** Every gadget maintains an isolated database partition; no data leakage across gadgets.\n\n#### 81. Plandex-Style Wasm Tree-Sitter Code Indexer Daemon\n* **Mental Model:** Navigates massive 20M+ token codebases without context window blowups.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Runs `web-tree-sitter` in WebAssembly inside a background Dynamic Worker, maintaining an AST symbol graph in SQLite.\n* **Invariants:** The agent queries exact symbol references instead of feeding raw files into the prompt.\n\n#### 82. Domain-Specific Durable Daemons\n* **Mental Model:** Background data engines combining stateful SQLite memory with autonomous workflow loops.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Runs in the background across domains: Finance (Ledger Reconciler), Legal (Citation Grapher), Logistics (Customs Tariff Matrix).\n* **Invariants:** Operates continuously in the background with zero CPU or token drag on active chat sessions.\n\n#### 83. Modular Extensions Architecture\n* **Mental Model:** The atomic Lego bricks of the platform.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Extensions bundle background daemons, custom viewports, linters, and MCP tools into installable packages.\n* **Invariants:** Extensions can be added to any project kind to unlock specialized vertical capabilities.\n\n#### 84. Auto-Generated Stateless MCP v2 Endpoints for Daemons \u0026 Gadgets\n* **Mental Model:** Every micro-app and daemon is immediately programmable by AI agents.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Automatically exposes `/mcp` endpoints wrapping internal SQLite schemas using Cloudflare MCP SDK v2.\n* **Invariants:** Agents query and mutate gadget state using standardized tool calls without custom API code.\n\n#### 85. Bidirectional MCP-UI Real-Time Canvas Streaming\n* **Mental Model:** The agent observes user interactions on the visual canvas.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Canvas iframe events (clicks, form submits, table edits) stream into the agent\u0027s observation loop over WebSockets.\n* **Invariants:** Actions taken in the UI trigger autonomous agent reactions without manual chat prompting.\n\n#### 86. Generative In-Chat Dynamic UI Widgets\n* **Mental Model:** Interactive widgets inside the chat feed (Google Search AI Mode style).\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** The model streams structured UI components (date pickers, sliders, approval cards) directly into the message feed.\n* **Invariants:** Widget inputs return structured payloads into the active turn without typing text.\n\n---\n\n## PHASE 7: Asymmetric Workflows, Inbound Queues \u0026 Telephony\n\n#### 87. 3-Class Workflow Taxonomy\n* **Mental Model:** Clean operational separation between business automation, studio tools, and agent tasks.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Classifies workflows as: Class 1 (Company Automations), Class 2 (Vertical Extensions), or Class 3 (Ephemeral Tasks).\n* **Invariants:** Establishes distinct trigger origins, spend allowances, and failure alert paths.\n\n#### 88. Asymmetric Subagent Topology (Verbs vs. Nouns)\n* **Mental Model:** Prevents over-engineering subagent architectures.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Subagents are ephemeral execution functions (\"verbs\") inside workflows; only Parent Agents are persistent entities (\"nouns\") managing threads and UI.\n* **Invariants:** Subagents do not own threads, manage session trees, or execute UI state changes.\n\n#### 89. Slimmed-Down `SubagentContext`\n* **Mental Model:** Eliminates step serialization crashes in Cloudflare Workflows.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Exposes only `ai`, `fs`, `cli`, `vault`, and `step`. Strips thread creation, WebSocket handles, and session bloat.\n* **Invariants:** All data crossing step boundaries is strictly JSON-serializable.\n\n#### 90. Repomix-Style Chunked Subagent Workflow with Branch Accumulator\n* **Mental Model:** Reliable multi-step software implementation that never hits output token truncation.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** Two-pass workflow: generates compressed repo map $\\rightarrow$ selects files $\\rightarrow$ implements atomic chunk $\\rightarrow$ commits. Branch accumulator automatically tracks newly created files.\n* **Invariants:** Each chunk modifies only 1–3 files, staying well under LLM generation limits.\n\n#### 91. Cloudflare Workflows Harness Pattern\n* **Mental Model:** The AI writes pure business logic; the platform handles deployment plumbing.\n* **Underlying Mechanics:** The agent writes