      "text": "This is a fundamental architectural realization that breaks the traditional bias that *\"Git is only for programmers.\"*\n\nUnder the hood, **Git is not a coding tool—it is a content-addressed versioning engine for files.** A Git commit tree does not care whether a file contains TypeScript, a multi-sheet financial model in Excel (`.xlsx`), raw transaction ledgers (`.csv`), or a 100-page commercial lease (`.md` / `.docx`).\n\nIn fact, for the majority of **Vertical Cowork Studios (\"Harvey for X\")**, the `/workspace/` directory contains **zero code**.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Inversion: Work is Data (`/workspace/`), Code is Machinery (`/.avos/`)\n\nIn non-coding verticals, the relationship between code and work is inverted:\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                                 THE WORKSPACE SPLIT IN VERTICAL COWORK                                 │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 📁 `/workspace/` \u003d THE PROJECT DELIVERABLE CANVAS (What the Human Cares About)                        │\n│ • In Finance (`finance_grid`): `dcf_valuation.xlsx`, `T12_actuals.csv`, `portfolio_comps.json`         │\n│ • In Law (`doc_studio`):        `master_services_agreement.docx`, `exhibit_a.md`, `title_deed.pdf`     │\n│ • In Clinics (`clinical_soap`): `patient_chart_402.md`, `lab_blood_panel.csv`                         │\n│ • In Logistics (`freight_hub`): `bill_of_lading_vessel42.csv`, `customs_manifest.json`                 │\n│ ➡️ Versioned by Cloudflare Artifacts (Git for Agents). Every edit is an immutable commit.              │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ ⚙️ `/.avos/` \u003d THE ENGINE \u0026 SKILLS (The ONLY Place Where Code Lives)                                   │\n│ • `/.avos/shared/skills/xlsx-formula-engine.ts` (The code that recalculates the Excel file).           │\n│ • `/.avos/shared/skills/delaware-statute-linter.ts` (The code that audits the lease).                  │\n│ • `/.avos/shared/workflows/nightly-reconcile.ts` (The background automation pipeline).                 │\n│ • `/.avos/agents/legal-operator/SOUL.md` (The agent instructions).                                     │\n│ ➡️ The client never touches this code. The AI uses this machinery to manipulate the workspace files.    │\n└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. How Cloudflare Artifacts Handles Non-Code Projects\n\nBecause Cloudflare Artifacts runs natively at the edge (Zig-to-WASM Git in Durable Objects), it versions non-code deliverables seamlessly:\n\n#### A. Structured Text, CSV, and Markdown\n* Files like `T12_actuals.csv` or `agreement.md` are native Git text objects.\n* When the AI recalculates a column or patches an indemnity clause, Artifacts computes an exact line-by-line diff.\n* The user scrubs the turn history like a time machine and clicks **`[⏪ Rollback Sheet to Turn 3]`**.\n\n#### B. Spreadsheets (`.xlsx`), Word Docs (`.docx`), and Binary Assets\n* Binary files are content-addressed by their SHA-256 hash inside Cloudflare Artifacts.\n* When an agent edits an Excel sheet using an internal script (like `xlsx` / `mammoth`), the updated workbook commits as a new version.\n* The frontend uses your **Multi-Format File Viewers** to render the visual delta:\n  * For Excel: Displays a before/after cell comparison grid.\n  * For Word/Contracts: Displays side-by-side legal redlines.\n\n---\n\n### 3. \"Pull Request Review Cards\" Become \"Deliverable Change Proposals\"\n\nIn a team of lawyers, underwriters, or clinicians, people don\u0027t do \"code reviews.\" They do **Deliverable Approvals**:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 📬 DELIVERABLE CHANGE PROPOSAL #14 (Rendered in Tier 1 Team Room)                                       │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 👤 Author: @Associate \u0026 @FinancialAnalystAgent                         [ 🌿 branch:update-cap-rates ]   │\n│ File: `portfolio/valuation_model.xlsx`                                                                  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 🤖 **Agent Rationale:**                                                                                 │\n│ \"Adjusted terminal cap rate from 6.0% to 6.5% to reflect Q3 interest rate projections.                  │\n│  Net Present Value (NPV) adjusted from $14.2M ──► $12.8M. Sensitivity matrix updated.\"                  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 🔍 **Visual Sheet Delta:**                                                                              │\n│ • Cell `D14` (Terminal Cap): `6.0%`  ──►  `6.5%`                                                        │\n│ • Cell `G22` (Unlevered IRR): `14.2%` ──►  `12.9%`                                                      │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ [ ✅ Accept \u0026 Update Master Valuation ]       [ 👁️ Open in Spreadsheet Grid ]       [ 💬 Request Recalc ]│\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\nWhen the Managing Director or Senior Partner taps **`[Accept \u0026 Update Master Valuation]`**:\n1. Cloudflare Artifacts executes an atomic fast-forward Git merge on `main`.\n2. The master `valuation_model.xlsx` in the project is updated.\n3. The live **`SpreadsheetFormulaGrid`** canvas updates in 150ms for everyone in the room.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Updating the Master Plan Mental Model\n\nIn the Master Architecture Specification, ensure this invariant is recorded:\n\n\u003e **The Artifacts Invariant:**  \n\u003e **`/workspace/` is the Deliverable Canvas (agnostic to file type).** It stores the primary work product of the project—which may be TypeScript source code (`product_dev`), financial spreadsheets (`finance_grid`), legal contract packages (`doc_studio`), architectural specification PDFs (`plan_spec`), or customer lead data (`growth_engine`).  \n\u003e **`/.avos/` is the sole repository of agent machinery.** It houses the executable scripts, compiled skills, background workflows, and `SOUL.md` directives that inspect, parse, and mutate the workspace deliverables.\n\nThis distinction is what allows your platform to serve a solo developer building an Astro website **and** an investment banking team underwriting a $50M commercial real estate deal using the exact same underlying Git engine, Durable Objects, and execution ladder.",
