      "text": "This completely unblocks real-world adoption. \n\nIn real business operations, **no medical clinic, law firm, or consultancy will ever abandon Google Calendar or Microsoft Outlook to use a proprietary calendar silo inside an AI platform.** \n\nBy making the Unified Calendar a **Space-Shared MCP Connector** mapped to a logical alias (`ctx.connectors.use(\"primary_calendar\")`), AVOS connects directly to the real world:\n* A dental clinic maps it to **Google Workspace**.\n* An enterprise law firm maps it to **Microsoft 365 / Outlook**.\n* A privacy-focused boutique maps it to **CalDAV / Fastmail**.\n* A new business with zero external accounts uses an **Edge-Native SQLite Fallback**.\n\n```\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                               THE SPACE-SHARED CALENDAR CONNECTOR MESH                                 │\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 📞 Voice Agent (`kind: \"voice_agent\"`) ──┐                                                            │\n│ 💬 WhatsApp Bot (`kind: \"customer_bot\"`) ──┼──► `const cal \u003d await ctx.connectors.use(\"primary_cal\");` │\n│ ⚖️ Legal Desk (`kind: \"doc_studio\"`)    ──┤    `await cal.call(\"book_slot\", { startTime, client });`  │\n│ 📱 Executive Copilot (Telegram)        ──┘                                                            │\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                                                    │ (Resolved via SpaceDO Binding Matrix)\n                                                    ▼\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                        PLUGGABLE THIRD-PARTY CALENDAR PROVIDERS (Composio / MCP)                       │\n├──────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────┤\n│ 1. Google Calendar   │ 2. Microsoft Outlook / 365  │ 3. CalDAV / Apple / Fastmail│ 4. Edge SQLite VFS  │\n│ (Google Workspace)   │ (Microsoft Graph API)       │ (Standard RFC 4791)         │ (Default fallback)  │\n├──────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────────────┼─────────────────────┤\n│ • Auto-creates Meet. │ • Auto-creates Teams link.  │ • Privacy / Self-hosted.    │ • Zero-setup fresh  │\n│ • Syncs to Android/iOS│ • Corporate enterprise sync│ • Air-gapped compatible.    │   spaces ($0 cost). │\n└──────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Real-World Problem: External API Latency \u0026 The Double-Booking Race\n\nExternal APIs (Google Calendar, Microsoft Graph) take **300ms to 800ms** to execute a booking. \n\nIf two customers call your AI Phone Desk at the exact same millisecond:\n1. Caller A asks for Friday at 2:00 PM $\\rightarrow$ Google API says \"Slot is free\".\n2. Caller B asks for Friday at 2:00 PM $\\rightarrow$ Google API says \"Slot is free\" (because Caller A\u0027s event hasn\u0027t finished writing yet!).\n3. Both callers are promised 2:00 PM. Result: **Catastrophic Double-Booking.**\n\n#### The Solution: The Edge \"Slot-Hold\" Mutex (`ConcurrencyDO`)\nBefore calling external calendar APIs, the agent acquires an ephemeral **15-Second Edge Reservation Lock**:\n\n```\n[ Customer requests: Friday 2:00 PM ]\n                 │\n                 ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 1. EDGE SLOT-HOLD MUTEX (`ConcurrencyDO`)                                   │\n│    `lock.acquire(\"calendar:hold:2026-09-18T14:00:00Z\", { ttlMs: 15000 })`   │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ • Caller 1: ✅ LOCK GRANTED.                                                │\n│ • Caller 2 (10ms later): ❌ LOCK DENIED.                                     │\n│   AI immediately tells Caller 2: \"2:00 PM is currently being reserved.      │\n│   How about 2:30 PM instead?\"                                               │\n└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n                 │\n                 ▼\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ 2. WRITE TO EXTERNAL PROVIDER (Google / Microsoft via Composio)             │\n│    `cal.call(\"create_event\", { startTime: \"2026-09-18T14:00:00Z\" })`       │\n│    • Once confirmed by Google, the edge lock is released.                   │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Two-Way Inbound Sync (When the Doctor Moves an Event on iPhone)\n\nIf a doctor opens the Google Calendar app on their iPhone and moves Friday\u0027s 2:00 PM appointment to 4:00 PM:\n1. Google/Microsoft fires an **Inbound Push Notification Webhook** to AVOS:\n   `POST https://webhooks.avos.app/v1/:spaceId/calendar-push`\n2. The **Edge Webhook Router** validates the provider secret and enqueues the event into `AUTOMATIONS_QUEUE`.\n3. A **Tier 3 Dynamic Workflow** consumes the event, updates any active project journal tasks, and pings the patient automatically over WhatsApp:\n   \u003e *\"Hi John, Dr. Smith rescheduled your appointment to Friday at 4:00 PM. Does this time still work for you?\"*\n\n---\n\n### 3. Personal Calendar Protection vs. Business Availability\n\nWhat happens if Dr. Smith has a **personal family event** (e.g. *\"Kid\u0027s Soccer Game\"*) on their personal calendar that isn\u0027t on the public business calendar?\n\nThe connector system supports **Multi-Calendar Availability Checks with Title Masking**:\n* When a public customer calls, the agent queries availability across **both** the Space-Shared Business Calendar AND the Doctor\u0027s Personal Calendar (via their User-Personal connector).\n* **Privacy Invariant:** The personal event\u0027s title is **cryptographically masked** before entering the agent\u0027s reasoning turn. The agent only receives `BUSY` for that window—it never learns the private event\u0027s name, notes, or location.\n\n---\n\n### 4. What This Updates in the Master Plan\n\n1. **Deprecate Rigid SQLite Calendar Silos:** Remove hardcoded calendar tables from `SpaceDO`. Replace them with the **Standardized Calendar Connector Interface** (`ctx.connectors.use(\"primary_calendar\")`).\n2. **Pluggable Calendar Providers:** Spaces can seamlessly bind to Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, CalDAV, or the default in-memory SQLite fallback.\n3. **15-Second Edge Slot-Hold Locks:** Prevents double-booking race conditions during high-volume voice call spikes while external third-party APIs process.\n4. **Automatic Video Links:** When booking on Google or Microsoft, the connector automatically appends Google Meet or Microsoft Teams links to the event payload.",
